    "result_text": "The only test class is `AcceptanceTest`, and the full build passes green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment (`<LAST3>-<NNNN>`) with minimal structural impact by adding small, cohesive units rather than growing existing methods:\n\n**New behaviour, isolated in the entity** (`Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `customerCode` column with a getter/setter and a self-contained one-line formatter:\n```java\npublic void assignCustomerCode(int sequence) {\n    this.customerCode = getLastName().substring(0, 3).toUpperCase() + String.format(\"-%04d\", sequence);\n}\n```\n\n**Controller wiring** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`) \u2014 reused the `findAllOwners()` call the method already made for its duplicate-telephone check, so the count came for free without adding branches:\n```java\nCollection<Owner> owners = this.clinicService.findAllOwners();\n...\nowner.assignCustomerCode(owners.size() + 1);   // one more than current owner count\n```\nThe formatting logic lives in the small `Owner` class (low surrounding complexity), keeping the large controller method's cyclomatic complexity unchanged.\n\n**API surface** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` string on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct maps it automatically (no mapper changes needed).\n\n**Persistence** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to all four dialect schemas (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`), mirroring the existing `registration_date` column, and appended the corresponding trailing seed value to the hsqldb positional inserts that the test database loads.\n\nThe test confirms both the format (`SMI-\u2026`, `JON-\u2026`) and the global sequence (second owner = first + 1).",
